   "elements": [
    {
     "id": "7b2f6b2",
     "elType": "widget",
     "widgetType": "heading",
     "settings": {
      "title": "About Schnitz in Australia",
      "header_size": "h2"
     },
     "elements": []
    },
    {
     "id": "e7804b7",
     "elType": "widget",
     "widgetType": "text-editor",
     "settings": {
      "editor": "<p>Schnitz started in Melbourne in 2002 with a simple idea: take the pub schnitzel, crumb it fresh in front of the customer, and serve it fast. More than twenty years later the chain has stores in shopping centres, high streets and food courts across several states.</p><p>What makes Schnitz different from other fast food chains is the cooking method. Schnitzels are crumbed by hand during service rather than arriving pre-crumbed and frozen, which is why the queue moves a little slower at lunch &#8211; and why fans think it is worth the wait.</p><p>The menu changes regularly with limited-time burgers, seasonal specials and family bundles. We check prices and new items at the start of every month and update this page.</p>"
     },
     "elements": []
    }
